        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: തലക്കെട്ട്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തലക്കെട്ട് — talakkeṭṭŭ — \"a headline; a title\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പത്രത്തിലെ വലിയ തലക്കെട്ട് ഞാൻ വായിച്ചു. patrattile valiya talakkeṭṭŭ ñān vāyiccu. I read the big headline in the newspaper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literally a head-band: the line tied across the top of a story or a chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തലക്കെട്ട് (talakkeṭṭŭ) is a native Dravidian compound of തല (tala), \"head\" (DEDR 3103), and കെട്ട് (keṭṭŭ), \"a tying, a band\", the noun of കെട്ടുക, \"to tie\" (DEDR 1147)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
