          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പത്രാധിപർ — patrādhipar — \"an editor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പത്രാധിപർ ലേഖകന്റെ റിപ്പോർട്ട് വായിച്ചു. patrādhipar lēkhakanṟe ṟippōrṭṭŭ vāyiccu. The editor read the correspondent's report."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The -ർ ending marks respect, so one editor is പത്രാധിപർ (patrādhipar); the plainer പത്രാധിപൻ is heard too."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പത്രാധിപർ (patrādhipar) is built from two Sanskrit words: patra, \"a leaf, a written sheet\", which gave പത്രം (patraṁ), \"a newspaper\", and adhipa, \"a ruler, a commander\" (Monier-Williams). The editor is the chief of the paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
