          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വായനക്കാരൻ (vāyanakkāran) is a Malayalam compound of വായന (vāyana), \"reading\", the noun of വായിക്കുക, \"to read\", and the ending -ക്കാരൻ, \"one who does it\". The verb is usually traced to Sanskrit vāc, \"speech\": reading was first reading aloud."
            }
